{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Nanda","html":"<article id='thag2.19'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 2.19 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 2.19 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Dukanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Twos </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Dutiyavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Two </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Nandattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Nanda </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Ayoniso manasikārā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Because of focusing on the wrong things, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>maṇḍanaṁ anuyuñjisaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I was addicted to ornamentation. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Uddhato capalo cāsiṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I was vain, fickle, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>kāmarāgena aṭṭito. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>racked by desire for pleasures of the senses. </span></span></p>\n<p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Upāyakusalenāhaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>But with the help of the Buddha, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>buddhenādiccabandhunā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the Kinsman of the Sun, so skilled in means, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yoniso paṭipajjitvā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I practiced rationally and extracted </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>bhave cittaṁ udabbahin”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>attachment to continued existence from my mind. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Nando thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
